ReScript File
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// The one shape the line-break rule gets wrong, pinned deliberately.')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('//')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// A type parameter list wrapped so that `<` opens a line is indistinguishable')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// from a JSX element to a regular lexer: `array` ⏎ `<int>` and `count` ⏎')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// `<div>` are the same token sequence. bsc tells them apart because it knows it')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// is parsing a type; this lexer has no such context and reads both as JSX.')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('//')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// Accepted rather than fixed, because:')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('//   - `rescript format` collapses `array` ⏎ `<int>` back to `array<int>`, so')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('//     the shape does not survive in formatted code;')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('//   - the damage stays inside the one declaration — the bindings after it below')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('//     parse normally, via structureItemRecover;')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('//   - the alternative is losing JSX in statement position, which is the far')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('//     commoner shape (every `@react.component let make` body).')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('//')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// The whole family is affected, not just `let` annotations — return types and')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// module bodies wrap the same way. The gold records two error elements. If a')
  PsiComment(LINE_COMMENT)('// future change gives the lexer type context, this fixture is the one to flip.')
